  "narrative": {
    "intro": "South Carolina has $72.4M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 217 awards with an average award size of $334K, and obligations fell 99.3% year over year. Year-by-year context shows much larger past totals: FY22 was $7.2B, FY23 was $10.1B, FY24 was $10.6B, FY25 was $8.3B, and FY26 was $9.8B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer in FY2027 to date, with $70.7M obligated. The next-largest buying agencies are the Department of Justice with $1.9M and the Department of Homeland Security with $80.3K. Couriers and Express Delivery Services and All Other Business Support Services are the top industries, receiving $25.9M and $25M respectively. FEDERAL EXPRESS CORPORATION and FEDEX SUPPLY CHAIN DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM, INC. are the top vendors, with $25.1M and $25M respectively. The data are partial, fiscal year to date totals, and reflect obligations rather than completed contract performance.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal buying in South Carolina this year?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $70.7M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Justice obligated $1.9M, and all other listed agencies contributed much smaller amounts, including two agencies with $0. Couriers and Express Delivery Services received $25.9M and All Other Business Support Services received $25M, showing industry concentration in logistics and support services. FEDERAL EXPRESS CORPORATION and FEDEX SUPPLY CHAIN DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM, INC. together account for roughly half of the state total in FY2027 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What changed compared with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 99.3% year over year in FY2027 to date. Prior fiscal years were larger: FY22 was $7.2B, FY23 was $10.1B, FY24 was $10.6B, FY25 was $8.3B, and FY26 was $9.8B. FY2027 to date is $72.4M, which is a partial, fiscal year to date total. The award count for FY2027 to date is 217 with an average award size of $334K."
      }
    ]
